ns for the next tick/owner: (a) run a real gitreins judge for QA-AUGER-13 on current main, then bind detail.evidence[].run_id to that fresh run id; (b) rule that a QA row's provenance may cite the row whose work it verified, and encode that in the audit's contract; (c) drop QA-AUGER-13's complete status if no same-task verdict exists. Until one is chosen, hosted CI stays red on the audit test (see INT-CI-001).\n\nNAMED BLOCKER, NOT CLOSED (foreman, 2026-11-20): the dispatched worker read scripts/audit_board_evidence.py and refused to fabricate a binding - no same-task verdict artifact exists for AUG-188, and the audit's real defect is upstream of any AUG-188 code change. Measured on merged main c4cf366: complete_rows=260 bound=116 unresolvable=1 missing=0, none_reason=143 (138 = no-verdict-artifact-for-task-id, 5 = cites-foreign-verdict), 19 bound rows carry a FAILED verdict, LABEL QA-AUGER-13 detail.evidence[].run_id=f3733f6c resolves to task AUG-151 -> UNRESOLVABLE foreign-citation. Same defect is the hosted-CI red, filed INT-CI-001. Blocker owner: next tick needs a decision on whether QA-AUGER-13/AUG-151 get an honest none: binding or a re-judge; the audit input cannot be fixed by editing the audit test.\n\nCOS VERIFICATION 2026-11-21T14:55Z (card manager, board restored at 9a9d987): AUG-188's fix is LANDED BUT THE ROW IS STILL PENDING — this is a reconciliation gap, not open work. The rebind landed at b3e8f17 (2026-11-20 20:50 local, \"AUG-188: rebind QA-AUGER-13 evidence to its own verdict ar...\"). Measured at HEAD 9a9d987, all four ACs:\nAC1 PASS — `.venv/bin/python scripts/audit_board_evidence.py` prints `label_defects=0` and ends `RESULT: OK` (rows=297 verdicts=182).\nAC2 PASS — `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_board_evidence_audit.py -q` -> 17 passed in 1.36s.\nAC3 PASS — QA-AUGER-13 cites run 3621b077 only; `.gitreins/history/2026-11-18/3621b077/verdict.json` records task_id QA-AUGER-13 (no foreign citation remains; f3733f6c is gone from the row).\n