+ {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-189", "title": "The gate's pytest arm runs under whichever python3 is first on PATH, so a clean tree grades RED for an absent dev dependency (collection errors), not for the diff", "detail": {"fingerprint": "4b98797fdeb8085358db5aa11be836586d44a479ded90225e33ba1ba14e1c018"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "COS card-manager 2026-11-20T14:55Z, filed on the promise made by the 2026-11-20T06:45Z pass (handoff open thread 1) and re-measured before filing. Measured at origin/main c7094d9 on this host: `python3` resolves differently per shell (the agent shell gets 3.14.9 via a hermes install venv, which HAS lxml+tomllib; /usr/bin/python3 is 3.14.4 and does NOT have lxml), and tests/gate.sh calls bare `python3 -m pytest` with no interpreter selection or naming. Consequence measured today at 06:23Z and reproduced now: a board-only commit attempt ran the full gate, the pytest arm died in 3.53s with 4 collection ERRORs (lxml in tests/test_xsd_conformance.py; tomllib in tests/test_packaging.py and tests/test_packaging_wheel.py; tests/test_verdict_hygiene.py also errored), and the commit was made with hooks bypassed and the bypass disclosed in the body. Proof artifacts already on disk: .gitreins/logs/guard-20261120T062345.212554Z.log and .gitreins/logs/guard-20261120T064011.062723Z.log. The repo's own .venv (3.11.15) runs the same suite green (805 passed / 2 skipped per the AUG-151 wave note), so the RED said nothing about the tree. This is the inverse of AUG-130 (which fixed PASS-on-skipped-arm): here the gate FAILS a tree it never really tested, and the asymmetry between pass and fail is not designed, it is PATH-dependent. Filing is deliberately cheap to verify: AC1's falsifier is a --collect-only probe, not the 994s suite.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "AC1 FALSIFIER, MEASURED 2026-11-20 AT ORIGIN/MAIN c7094d9: the gate's pytest arm inherits the ambient interpreter, so an interpreter without the dev extra turns a clean tree RED. Run `/usr/bin/python3 -m pytest -q --collect-only tests/test_xsd_conformance.py` and it prints `1 error during collection` with exit code 2 (`ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'lxml'`), while `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q --collect-only tests/test_xsd_conformance.py` expects exit 0 and a collected count. FAILIF: both interpreters agree, which means the gate gained an interpreter guard and this row is already satisfied.\n\nAC2 THE GATE SELECTS AND NAMES ITS INTERPRETER: `bash tests/gate.sh` run with an ambient PATH whose first python3 lacks the dev extra prints a line naming the interpreter it chose (a checkout-local interpreter is preferred when one exists), and the same invocation over a board-only or docs-only diff ends in GATE PASS or an explicitly DEGRADED pass that names its skipped required arm, never GATE FAIL for a dependency. FAILIF: the run still fails on collection errors from an interpreter the tree does not own, or no line names the chosen interpreter.\n\nAC3 NEGATIVE CONTROL, THE FAIL-CLOSED POLICY MUST NOT REGRESS: with AUGER_ALLOW_SKIPPED_ARMS unset and an interpreter that genuinely cannot import pytest, `bash tests/gate.sh` still exits nonzero and prints GATE FAIL naming the pytest arm as a required arm that did not run (the AUG-130 policy). FAILIF: GATE PASS with the suite never executed, i.e. the interpreter selection turned a true red into a silent skip.\n\nAC4 REGRESSION TEST: a committed case in the gate's own self-test asserts the selection rule (a checkout-local interpreter wins over the ambient one) so a later edit cannot re-introduce bare `python3`. Verify: `bash tests/test_gate_mode.sh` exits 0 and its output contains a case naming the interpreter selection, and `bash tests/docs_check.sh` exits 0 so documentation of the gate still matches the script. FAILIF: both scripts exit 0 but no case in the self-test names interpreter selection, i.e. the rule is unproven by test and this AC has not landed.\n\nGATE ARM: Run `bash tests/gate.sh`; expect the summary block to name the interpreter it selected.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-20T14:37:22+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-20T17:50:23+00:00", "foreman_note": "LANDED, NOT CLOSED (foreman, 2026-11-20): commit 900de88 on main (worktree /home/kara/worktrees/auger-AUG-189, branch wt/AUG-189, base 4da3a39). Verified in-tree before merge: tests/test_gate_mode.sh 5/5 PASS including the new 'AUG-189 interpreter selection: PASS' case, tests/docs_check.sh PASS, pytest -q tests/test_xsd_conformance.py 12 passed under .venv. 'gitreins task complete AUG-189' marked the task complete but wrote NO .gitreins/history/2026-11-20/<run>/verdict.json - the only runs for today are AUG-151 x2, AUG-186, AUG-171, AUG-155. Without an artifact I cannot bind evidence_run_id, and TR-251 forbids closing on a claim, so the row stays pending. Re-run 'gitreins task complete AUG-189' on a quiet box to produce the artifact, then close with that run id.", "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null, "sessions": null, "type": null}
